#====================================================================
# E213 Draft - CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE may be declared but unsupported
#====================================================================

id:                     E270
trigger_tool:           ctest|bench
phase:                  runtime
error_signature:        clock_gettime\(CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE.*EINVAL|bench -s.*timeout|measure_execution_time.*start_over

severity:               2
category:               platform_compat
match_keywords:         CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE, clock_gettime, EINVAL, FFTW,
                        measure_execution_time, start_over, CLOCK_MONOTONIC, OHOS
title:                  CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE may be declared but unsupported at runtime

root_cause:             Some libc headers expose CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE even though
                        the kernel rejects clock_gettime(CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE, ...)
                        with EINVAL. FFTW 3.3.10 selects this clock when the
                        macro is defined and does not check the return code.
                        Invalid timing samples can repeatedly restart planner
                        measurement and prevent default FFTW_MEASURE planning
                        from terminating.
affected_scope:         FFTW 3.3.10 and software that treats a declared
                        CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE macro as proof of runtime support.
verification_cmd:       Probe CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE and CLOCK_MONOTONIC return codes,
                        rebuild, then run unchanged CTest entries 32x64 and ib256.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           source-patch
rec_description:        Check clock_gettime(CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE, ...) at runtime and
                        fall back to CLOCK_MONOTONIC only when it fails. Preserve
                        the upstream clock on platforms where it is supported and
                        leave the upstream test arguments unchanged.
rec_command:            Patch kernel/cycle.h to check the clock_gettime return value.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               none

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      monotonic-clock
fallback_description:   Use CLOCK_MONOTONIC unconditionally in the existing
                        struct timespec timing branch when a runtime fallback is
                        not suitable for the target environment.
fallback_command:       Replace CLOCK_SGI_CYCLE with CLOCK_MONOTONIC in kernel/cycle.h.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          none

forbid_1_pattern:       -oestimate
forbid_1_reason:        Adding -oestimate changes the official benchmark planner mode.
forbid_1_consequence:   A fast diagnostic result would not prove the original upstream entry passed.

principles:             P007, P020

causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:               doc/E270.md
last_updated:           2026-07-24
source_event:           fftw 3.3.10 official CTest 32x64 on OHOS

authors:                 2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
source_pr:              1994
source_commit:          86629300381b97b23bc8c30da3385f7aacbeea01

